 I was thinking that some/all cursed scrolls should have a luck-dependent chance of doing something a bit different.

FLOOD:
A cursed scroll of flood should have a small, dungeon-level/luck-dependent chance of creating Lethe water under you instead of regular water.

This is good for several reasons:

1) more randomness
2) we could stand to have luck do more things
3) as you get deeper, the Lethe should feel like it has more pull on the dungeon
4) right now, the uncursed scroll is delectably worse than the cursed, because it can still do your square and is a serious inconvenience/drowning risk. this way, the cursed can still end up being nastier
5) scroll of flood replaced scroll of amnesia - this is a nice throwback to the old feature

DETECT TRAP:
the cursed scroll should have a 50% chance of creating (but keeping hidden or showing as gold) rnl(5) traps throughout the level.

This is good because:
1) it lets additional traps appear after level generation in a way that makes sense
2) more randomness = more fun
3) though it makes it more dangerous, it also suggests a possible use (e.x. you are hoping to create a certain type of trap)
4) again, lets the luck stat participate in more things

LIGHT:
the cursed scroll should have a 25% chance of summoning rnl(4) yellow lights and/or black lights near you

This is good because
1) more randomness
2) lets luck participate
3) lets these monsters have a role to play beyond the first few levels

CONFUSE MONSTER:

the cursed scroll should have a chance of also confusing nearby pets
also, wielded intelligent artifacts that can blast you have a small luck-dependent chance of getting confused and blasting you (the confusion does involve your hands, it is kinda a monster, and you are holding it)

This is good because:
1) now you have to be more careful if using this to confuse yourself before reading other scrolls
2) the effect makes sense - the cursed version confuses all the people you don't want to confuse

STINKING CLOUD:
the cursed scroll should have a chance of also creating a few gas-spores and rotten eggs

This is good because:
1) "you smell rotten eggs"
2) gas spores are fun
3) suggests a potential use - you can try to unturn dead the eggs. maybe you got something good?

Anyways, I think that implementing some or all of these (my favorites are definitely the first 3) would not seriously effect the difficulty, would add more randomness, fits thematically, and increases fun.

